<td><h2>DN Media Group – Changes to pension scheme</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2026-10-01 08:33:51</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>DN Media Group has reached a formal agreement with employee representatives on changes to the group's pension arrangements in Norway.<br><br>The agreement entails that the company's defined benefit pension scheme will be discontinued. Employees directly affected by the change will receive individual compensation. At the same time, contribution rates in the defined contribution scheme will be increased for all employees in Norway.<br><br>The changes are expected to be approximately cost-neutral. The discontinuation of the defined benefit scheme will trigger a one-off accounting effect, currently estimated at NOK 34–42 million, expected to be recognised in Q4 2026. The estimate is preliminary and subject to final actuarial calculations.<br><br>The new pension arrangement will take effect from 1 January 2027.<br><br>For further information, please contact: Remi Eliassen, CFO, DN Media Group Remi.Eliassen@dngroup.com</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
